id: pm-g7cup8
title: Refuse assignment-only shell lists and command terminators
description: "PR1559 full review found that RESULT=passed; bypasses the assignment scanner and can be recorded as a successful test. The same gap covers assignment-only lists separated by semicolon, and/or, pipeline or background operators. Recognize these lists while retaining quoted or escaped operators, substitutions and actual executable commands."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-23T15:09:05.447Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T15:17:51.402Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-23T15:17:50.432Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-23T15:17:50.432Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 30
parent: pm-gh1555
risk: low
confidence: high
resolution: "Recognize unquoted shell list separators at the shared SDK command-admission boundary while preserving quoted/escaped values, substitutions and real executables; registration, legacy execution and recovery share this refusal."
expected_result: Assignment-only shell lists cannot create false pass evidence or mutate registration/history; actual executable lists continue to run.
actual_result: "138 linked regressions pass, including semicolon no-write controls and real later-command execution. Fresh npm/npx and Bun/bunx installs pass admission, recovery and SDK checks. Type, lint, docs links, generated surfaces, refreshed advisory feeds and all seven source-quality assurance assertions pass. Current-head hosted checks and review remain merge conditions."
comments[6]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-23T15:09:05.447Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: live search and open/in_progress reads plus complete3079-item strict all-status corpus found no active owner for this terminator defect. Full live parent metadata/comments and verified history were inspected; completed parents remain terminal. Source https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1559#discussion_r4360996939."
  "2026-10-23T15:09:58.380Z","harness:codex","Negative control: all six added semicolon cases fail on the previous scanner with no expected refusal;46 existing/preservation controls pass. The same lexical boundary permits assignment-only and/or, pipeline and background lists, so this child covers shell list separators together. Keep parsing linear, preserve quoted/escaped operators and decline interpreting substitutions or redirections."
  "2026-10-23T15:14:10.201Z","harness:codex","Verification:138 linked regressions pass across command admission, real CLI/SDK no-write refusal and recovery, and aggregate execution. Fresh packed consumers installed independently with npm and Bun pass semicolon, conditional, pipeline and background refusal through npx and bunx, with unchanged item/history bytes; structured recovery, literal paths and public SDK rejection also pass. Artifact SHA-256 f949e201c124641c3d2e3046bb8094463f679ce1a392560633633a8dce66a90f. Type checking, ESLint, public SDK/error snapshots, documentation links and100% docstring coverage pass. Repository source-quality assurance is still running; current-head hosted gates and renewed review remain merge conditions."
  "2026-10-23T15:14:18.162Z","harness:codex","Correction to the immediately preceding evidence comment: the actual packed artifact SHA-256 is 28813c9f7f1bdf36a996554aba24c84e68e217a84c3017383c205faf4e8e40c5; the prior digest was a transcription error. The install/behavior receipts pass for this actual artifact. Docstring-quality command passes; precise coverage percentages will be taken from the pending source-quality assurance result."
  "2026-10-23T15:15:09.739Z","harness:codex","Source-quality assurance passed its source, absence-tolerance, token-budget, context-intent, documentation and defect-evidence assertions, but the combined gate refused because the advisory receipt aged out during the extended review cycle. Refreshing both advisory feeds and rerunning the same assurance; no freshness or quality policy is relaxed."
  "2026-10-23T15:17:47.440Z","harness:codex","Final local gate evidence: fresh registry and OSV advisory collection passes for568 lockfile packages; the unchanged combined repository-static-quality assurance now passes all seven assertions.138 linked tests and fresh installed npm/npx and Bun/bunx acceptance pass. No deadlines, coverage thresholds, quality budgets or feed freshness requirements changed. Exact pushed-head CI, full coverage and renewed reviewer inventory remain merge conditions."
